<h1>How to Spot a Job Scam</h1>
<p>Fake recruitment offers can target freshers and experienced job seekers. Check the employer and vacancy carefully before sharing documents or making payments.</p>

<h2>1. Warning Signs</h2>
<ul>
<li>A recruiter promises guaranteed selection in exchange for money.</li>
<li>You are asked to pay a security deposit or recruitment fee to a personal account.</li>
<li>The offer arrives without a credible interview or selection process.</li>
<li>The recruiter uses suspicious email addresses or impersonates a known company.</li>
<li>You are pressured to act immediately without time to verify details.</li>
<li>The salary or benefits seem unusually attractive for the role and requirements.</li>
</ul>

<h2>2. Verify the Employer</h2>
<p>Visit the employer's official website independently. Find its careers page and check whether the vacancy, recruiter and contact details are genuine. Do not rely only on links sent in messages.</p>

<h2>3. Protect Your Information</h2>
<ul>
<li>Never share passwords, OTPs or banking PINs.</li>
<li>Do not install unknown apps at a recruiter's request.</li>
<li>Be careful when sharing identity documents or bank details.</li>
<li>Use official application portals whenever possible.</li>
</ul>

<h2>4. Before Paying Any Fee</h2>
<p>Read the official recruitment notification and verify whether a fee is authorised. Never pay a personal contact who claims they can guarantee selection or arrange an offer letter.</p>

<h2>5. If You Suspect a Scam</h2>
<div class="warning">
<strong>Stop communicating and preserve the evidence.</strong>
<p>Keep messages, phone numbers, receipts, payment details and screenshots. Contact your bank or payment provider quickly if you transferred money.</p>
</div>

<p>In India, report suspected cybercrime at <a href="https://cybercrime.gov.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">National Cyber Crime Reporting Portal</a>. If money has been lost to cyber fraud, call the national cybercrime helpline at <strong>1930</strong> as soon as possible.</p>

<h2>Final Checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li>Verify the vacancy on the official website.</li>
<li>Check the recruiter's identity.</li>
<li>Read the selection process and fee details.</li>
<li>Do not trust guaranteed-selection promises.</li>
<li>Keep records of all communications and payments.</li>
</ul>

